{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790468183307,"sessionID":"ses_f1fc909e3ffenldWD8cipIdpHJ","part":{"id":"prt_0e037ab7d001mQ2KeN5HXfZ2Ka","messageID":"msg_0e037a448001K53f7qAEHnNxW2","sessionID":"ses_f1fc909e3ffenldWD8cipIdpHJ","type":"reasoning","text":"Let me understand the key issues from the eval data:\n\n1. Seeds 2,3: die of starvation at max_depth 1, Xp:7\n2. Seeds 0,1: die to watch captain at max_depth 4, Xp:9\n3. Seed 4: reaches max_depth 11, progress 0.161 (best)\n4. Seed 5: petrified by cockatrice at max_depth 5\n\nThe core problem is that the bot gets stuck on dlvl 1 and dies of starvation before gaining enough experience or finding a way down. The best seed (4) reaches dlvl 11.\n\nLet me look at what seed 4 does differently. The key difference is that it reaches dlvl 11 while others get stuck at dlvl 1.\n\nLooking at the exploration logic, the `explore1` function is the main exploration driver. The bot needs to find and go down stairs. Let me check if there's an issue with the stair descent.\n\nLooking at `global_logic.py` `current_strategy`:\n- Milestone `BE_ON_FIRST_LEVEL` requires `blstats.experience_level >= 8`\n- After that, it tries to find Gnomish Mines, Sokoban, Minetown, etc.\n\nThe issue is that the bot needs to go down stairs to progress, but it may not be doing so effectively.\n\nLet me look at what happens when the bot is on dlvl 1. The `explore1` function should eventually find stairs down. But the bot might be getting stuck in loops or not prioritizing going down.\n\nActually, let me re-read the eval data more carefully. The progress score seems to be related to both survival and depth reached. Let me look at how progress is calculated.\n\nFrom the NLE framework, the `progress` score is likely based on depth and survival time. The formula might be something like: progress = (some function of max_depth, turns survived, experience level, etc.)\n\nLooking at the data:\n- Seed 4: progress 0.161, max_depth 11 - this is the best by far\n- Seeds 0,1: progress 0.117, max_depth 4\n- Seeds 2,3: progress 0.051, max_depth 1\n- Seed 5: progress 0.117, max_depth 5\n\nSo depth seems to be a major factor in the score. The bot needs to get deeper.\n\nThe most focused change would be to improve the bot's ability to descend stairs and explore deeper levels. Let me think about what's preventing it from going deeper.\n\nLooking at the `current_strategy` in `global_logic.py`, the milestone `BE_ON_FIRST_LEVEL` requires `experience_level >= 8`. But the bot needs to go down stairs to gain more experience. The problem might be that:\n\n1. The bot doesn't prioritize finding stairs down\n2. The bot gets stuck fighting monsters instead of descending\n3. Starvation kills the bot before it can reach exp level 8\n\nLet me look at the `explore1` function more carefully. It has a priority system for what tiles to visit. The priorities include:\n- Open neighbor doors\n- Search for things\n- Avoid stones and walls\n\nBut I don't see explicit prioritization of stairs down. The bot might be exploring side areas instead of going down.\n\nActually, looking at the `go_to_level_strategy` which is called from `current_strategy`, it uses `levels_to_explore_to_get_to` to find levels to explore. But for the first level, it just requires `experience_level >= 8` to proceed.\n\nWait, let me re-read the `current_strategy`:\n\n```python\nif self.milestone == Milestone.BE_ON_FIRST_LEVEL:\n    condition = lambda: self.agent.blstats.experience_level >= 8\n    level = (Level.DUNGEONS_OF_DOOM, 1)\n```\n\nSo the strategy stays on the first level until experience level 8. But how does the bot gain experience? By killing monsters. And the `fight2` strategy should handle combat.\n\nThe problem might be that the bot is not efficiently killing monsters, or not exploring enough of the level to find and kill monsters.\n\nLet me think about what change would have the most impact:\n\n1. **Improve stair descent**: Make the bot prioritize going down stairs once it's explored sufficiently\n2. **Fix starvation**: Make the bot eat more regularly\n3. **Improve combat**: Make the bot kill monsters faster\n\nLooking at the data more carefully:\n- Seeds 2,3 die at max_depth 1, Xp:7 of starvation - these bots never even reach exp level 8\n- Seeds 0,1 reach exp level 9 (Xp:9) at depth 4 but die to watch captain\n- Seed 4 reaches depth 11 - this one works best\n\nThe starvation deaths (seeds 2,3) are critical - the bot can't even survive long enough to gain levels. Let me check if the bot is eating at all.\n\nLooking at the `global_logic.py` `global_strategy`:\n```python\n.preempt(self.agent, [\n    self.offer_corpses().preempt(self.agent, [\n        self.agent.eat_corpses_from_ground().condition(lambda: self.agent.blstats.hunger_state >= Hunger.NOT_HUNGRY),\n    ]),\n])\n```\n\nAnd:\n```python\n.preempt(self.agent, [\n    self.agent.eat_corpses_from_ground().condition(lambda: self.agent.blstats.hunger_state >= Hunger.NOT_HUNGRY),\n    self.agent.eat_corpses_from_ground().every(5).condition(lambda: self.agent.blstats.hunger_state >= Hunger.NOT_HUNGRY),\n    self.agent.eat_from_inventory().every(5),\n])\n```\n\nSo the bot does have eating strategies. But the condition `hunger_state >= Hunger.NOT_HUNGRY` means it only eats when not hungry, which seems backwards... wait, let me check the Hunger enum.\n\nActually, looking more carefully, the `eat_corpses_from_ground` and `eat_from_inventory` strategies are preempted with conditions. Let me check the Hunger class.\n\nLet me also look at what's happening with the bot's food consumption. The starvation deaths suggest the bot isn't eating enough.\n\nActually, let me take a step back and think about this more holistically. The key observation is:\n\n1. Seed 4 reaches dlvl 11 with progress 0.161 - this is the outlier that does well\n2. Most other seeds get stuck at dlvl 1 and die of starvation\n3. Some reach dlvl 4-5 but die to monsters\n\nThe most impactful single change would be to ensure the bot can consistently get past dlvl 1 and descend to dlvl 2+. \n\nLooking at the exploration logic, I notice that `explore1` doesn't seem to have a specific priority for stairs down. The bot explores based on a priority map that favors unexplored territory, open doors, etc., but may not consistently find stairs.\n\nLet me check if there's a strategy for going down stairs. Looking at `go_to_level_strategy`, it uses `levels_to_explore_to_get_to` which for the first level just checks `experience_level >= 8`. But it doesn't explicitly go down stairs - it explores the current level.\n\nActually wait - I think the issue might be simpler. Let me look at the `eat_from_inventory` and `eat_corpses_from_ground` strategies and their conditions more carefully.\n\nLet me also check what `Hunger.NOT_HUNGRY` means and how the bot's hunger state progresses.\n\nLet me look at the Glyph module for Hunger:","time":{"start":1790468139901,"end":1790468183293}}}
