{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790468551462,"sessionID":"ses_f1fc909e3ffenldWD8cipIdpHJ","part":{"id":"prt_0e03dc50d001N8cqY66gjdZGdY","messageID":"msg_0e03dc021001hzHbEScZ3Bw7L0","sessionID":"ses_f1fc909e3ffenldWD8cipIdpHJ","type":"reasoning","text":"Interesting! The results show mixed performance:\n- Seed 0: progress 0.037, max_depth 1, killed by giant bat at Xp:6\n- Seed 1: progress 0.024, max_depth 1, killed by giant rat at Xp:4\n- Seed 2: progress 0.179, max_depth 5, killed by owlbear at Xp:10 (this is better than before!)\n- Seed 3: progress 0.037, max_depth 1, died of starvation\n- Seed 4: progress 0.037, max_depth 4, killed by little dog at Xp:6\n\nWait, seed 2 reached max_depth 5 with progress 0.179, which is better than the original parent-eval's seed 4 (0.161, depth 11). But the other seeds are performing worse - they're getting stuck at dlvl 1.\n\nThis is concerning. The change might be causing the bot to prioritize stairs down too aggressively, causing it to descend before it's ready (before finding enough food or killing enough monsters), leading to deaths at lower experience levels.\n\nLet me reconsider the approach. The priority of 1000 might be too high, causing the bot to descend stairs too early before it's sufficiently leveled or geared.\n\nLet me try a smaller priority value, or a different approach. Maybe I should only prioritize stairs down when the bot has sufficient experience or hitpoints, or when there's nothing else worth exploring.\n\nActually, looking at the results more carefully:\n- Seed 2: depth 5, progress 0.179 - this is actually quite good! The owlbear death at Xp:10 is reasonable.\n- Seeds 0,1,3,4: all stuck at depth 1 - this is worse than the original.\n\nThe issue is that the 1000 priority is too aggressive - it's causing the bot to go down stairs even when it's not ready, leading to deaths at dlvl 1 for some seeds, while others benefit from getting deeper.\n\nLet me reduce the priority or add a condition. Maybe I should only prioritize stairs down when:\n1. The bot has a minimum experience level\n2. The bot has sufficient hitpoints\n3. The bot has been exploring for a while without finding other interesting things\n\nOr maybe I should take a different approach entirely. Let me think about this.\n\nActually, the original bot without my change was scoring 0.112 average across 15 seeds. With my change and only 5 seeds, the average is (0.037 + 0.024 + 0.179 + 0.037 + 0.037) / 5 = 0.0588, which is worse. But seed 2 is much better (0.179 vs original ~0.117).\n\nThe problem is that the high priority for stairs down is causing some seeds to descend too early and die, while others benefit from getting deeper.\n\nLet me try a more moderate approach. Maybe I should add the stairs-down priority but with a lower value, or add conditions based on experience level or other factors.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the whole approach. The key issue is that the bot gets stuck on dlvl 1. Maybe instead of forcing stair descent, I should fix the underlying issue: why the bot can't survive on dlvl 1.\n\nLet me look at the original bot's performance again. The original 15-seed average was 0.112. The best seed reached 0.161 at depth 11. The worst seeds starved at depth 1.\n\nMy change made things worse for 4 out of 5 tested seeds. Let me try a different approach.\n\nInstead of adding a large priority boost for stairs down, let me try a smaller boost, or add it only under certain conditions.\n\nActually, let me try removing my change and thinking of a different hypothesis.\n\nWait, let me re-examine. The original parent-eval shows:\n- Seeds 0,1: progress 0.117, max_depth 4\n- Seeds 2,3: progress 0.051, max_depth 1, starvation\n- Seed 4: progress 0.161, max_depth 11\n- Seed 5: progress 0.117, max_depth 5\n\nSo originally, 2 seeds starve at depth 1, 2 seeds reach depth 4, 1 seed reaches depth 11, 1 seed reaches depth 5.\n\nWith my change and 5 seeds:\n- 2 seeds at depth 1 (starvation or monster death)\n- 1 seed at depth 4\n- 1 seed at depth 5 with progress 0.179\n- 1 seed at depth 1\n\nActually, 2 seeds at depth 1 is the same as before. But the progress scores are lower (0.037 vs 0.117 for the depth-1 seeds). And seed 2 is better at depth 5 with 0.179.\n\nLet me try a smaller priority value. Maybe 100 instead of 1000.","time":{"start":1790468539661,"end":1790468551457}}}
