{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790469779529,"sessionID":"ses_f1fc909e3ffenldWD8cipIdpHJ","part":{"id":"prt_0e0506e87001HIPFPUW1J0enfr","messageID":"msg_0e0506970001vukrOC5b2drJvk","sessionID":"ses_f1fc909e3ffenldWD8cipIdpHJ","type":"reasoning","text":"Let me add a food priority to the `to_search_func` function. I'll add priority for food objects (FOOD_CLASS glyphs) so the bot more frequently finds and picks up food.\n\nThe food priority should be added after the existing priority calculations and before the walkability/distance checks. I'll add a modest priority for food tiles.\n\nLet me also check what `G.FOOD_OBJECTS` contains - it's defined in `glyph.py` as food objects. But I need to check if the glyphs in `level.objects` are FOOD_CLASS. Let me use `utils.isin(level.objects, G.FOOD_OBJECTS)` or `utils.isin(level.objects, nh.FOOD_CLASS)` - actually, the observation's `glyphs` array contains the glyph IDs, and `G.FOOD_OBJECTS` is a frozenset of glyph IDs for food objects.\n\nWait, looking at `glyph.py`:\n```python\nFOOD_OBJECTS = frozenset({i for i in NORMAL_OBJECTS\n                          if ord(nh.objclass(nh.glyph_to_obj(i)).oc_class) == nh.FOOD_CLASS})\n```\n\nSo `G.FOOD_OBJECTS` contains glyph IDs for food objects. I can use `utils.isin(level.objects, G.FOOD_OBJECTS)` to check if a tile has food.\n\nBut actually, `level.objects` might not be populated yet when `explore1` runs. Let me check... `level.objects` is updated in `update_level`:\n```python\nmask = utils.isin(self.glyphs, G.MONS, G.PETS, G.BODIES, G.OBJECTS, G.STATUES)\nlevel.seen[mask] = True\nlevel.objects[mask] = self.glyphs[mask]\n```\n\nSo `level.objects` is set to the current glyphs. And `self.glyphs` is updated in `update`:\n```python\nself.blstats = BLStats(*self.last_observation['blstats'])\nself.glyphs = self.last_observation['glyphs']\n```\n\nSo `level.objects` should have the current glyphs, including food glyphs. I can use `utils.isin(level.objects, G.FOOD_OBJECTS)` to check for food.\n\nActually, let me use a simpler approach. I'll check `utils.isin(level.objects, nh.FOOD_CLASS)` or just check if the glyph is in `G.FOOD_OBJECTS`. Let me use `G.FOOD_OBJECTS` since it's already defined.\n\nWait, but `level.objects` contains glyph IDs, and `G.FOOD_OBJECTS` is a frozenset of glyph IDs. So `utils.isin(level.objects, G.FOOD_OBJECTS)` should work.\n\nLet me add the food priority. I'll add it after the existing priority calculations and before the walkability checks.","time":{"start":1790469762695,"end":1790469779518}}}
